note=f'''\n## Why the all-history lobster result changes\n\nPoint Dume SMCA contributes only 2021–2023 after protection. Its fixed-zone lobster log-ratio slope changes from −0.534 to −1.145 per year, with an estimated standard error of 0.104 rather than 0.231. That very short history therefore has greater influence after correction. A diagnostic omitting only this previously identified history gives a corrected pooled lobster trajectory of {convert(q.estimate):+.1f}% per year (95% interval {convert(q.low):+.1f} to {convert(q.high):+.1f}%). This is an influence check, not a proposed result-based exclusion. Its uncertainty remains difficult to estimate from three annual observations.\n\nThe LTER sheephead-biomass slopes also change markedly when fixed transects replace changing survey coverage: Campus Point −0.462 to +0.145 and Naples −0.257 to +0.230 log-ratio units/year. These are individual trajectories; the pooled sheephead trend remains uncertain. At Naples, the fixed reference transects have zero sheephead biomass in 2022 and 2023; reference transect AQUE 6, which lacks continuous coverage, contains positive biomass in those years. Its removal produces very large corrected ratios dependent on the retained additive constant. The fixed subset narrows the habitat represented and is not automatically a better population-wide estimate. This needs resolution before primary adoption.\n\nWithin the 140 early-start histories, corrected BH q-values are 0.041 for lobster density and both purple-urchin responses, 0.064 for kelp and 0.135 for red-urchin density. These do not justify choosing the cohort based on significance.\n\nhistory_examples.png/pdf: gray original; orange fixed survey units. Panels a–b show LTER sheephead biomass, c–d PISCO lobster density. Ratios include the frozen additive correction. Vertical dashed lines show protection year; horizontal dotted lines show equal protected/reference values. Curves connect observed survey years, including gaps, without imputing missing observations. Only modeled years are displayed; unused before-protection records and the designation year are omitted. These are descriptive annual ratios, not fitted recovery curves or confidence bands.\n'''
path.write_text(text+note)
